ission and processing, resulting in the server rejecting the request.\r\n\r\nThis tries to work around this problem by inferring, at the time of entry, whether an order is being back-dated or forward-dated (\"user-selected date\") or just relying on the default (i.e., the order date is the today). If the order date is today, we submit an order (and encounter) with no datetime, allowing the server side to fill in these datetime fields. Because they use the server timestamps, these timestamps should always be earlier or equal to the moment the encounter validation fires.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n<!-- Required if you are making UI changes. -->\r\n\r\n## Related Issue\r\n<!-- Paste the link to the Jira ticket here if one exists. -->\r\n<!-- https://issues.openmrs.org/browse/O3- -->\r\n\r\n## Other\r\n<!-- Anything not covered above -->\r\n","nextOffset":null,"truncated":["commentBodies was cut when the pull request was imported"]}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NVZmohJgWMbZspMScUuhSL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
